comments.message:
We should rather do:

```c
rc = encode_pldm_header_only_errno(...);
if (rc) {
   return rc;
}
```

```
rc = pack_pldm_header_errno(...);
if (rc) {
    return rc;
}
```

`-EAGAIN` is inappropriate here. The decode is successful but the response contained an erroneous completion code. The return value of the function _only_ corresponds to the success or failure of decoding the response. This should be:

```
rc = pldm_msg_has_error(msg, payload_length);
if (rc) {
    resp_data->completion_code = rc;
    return 0;
}
```

The caller then needs to check the `completion_code` member before proceeding to read the remaining members.
